# Past its boundary a scan reads only the rest of its line, and an empty line is a line of its own. Rows up to the end of
# the first 100 byte buffer, a buffer of nothing but newlines, then a newline and a last line of 100 bytes: the scan of
# the first buffer stops at the first empty line, so the last line is read once, by the scan it starts in.

